    "//Selkie": "Feature 31, the selkie (pack Prompt 47), in the heron's soft shape (hw_tgr_heron.json): the roll never names Far Territory in a hard field. Gates (StatChangeTrigger only): hw_switch_selkie {1,1}, vanilla IsNight {1,1}, vanilla Sheltered {0,0}, hw_selkie_clock at its max (SELKIE cooldown 288 = 3 days, grace 5 days). Roll: Nothing 75 against Selkie, whose BASE weight is 0 plus 25 for the Far Territory shore card (ftEnvShore) on the board (a CardDropChanceModifiers row, NotInHand and ExcludeInventory), minus the offering (up to -10) and Sanctuary (read only, up to -3): off the shore, or with Far Territory not installed (the card is missing, the row adds nothing), the Selkie collection's final weight is 0 or less and the game skips it, so Nothing always wins. The roll resets the clock wherever the player stands, so it is a chance per cooldown and only lands on the shore if the player is there when it fills. No target list names a Far Territory UID, so no load guard is needed (the event card holds only vanilla stats and Harsh Wilds stats). Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER.",
